questions.question:
Mobile app 3.6 handles every error response with:

const body = await res.json();
showBanner(String(body.message));

The API returned these three bodies the same afternoon:

(A) POST /enrollments -> 400
{"statusCode":400,"message":["email must be an email","courseId should not be empty"],"error":"Bad Request"}

(B) POST /enrollments -> 409
{"type":"https://api.codedev.test/problems/already-enrolled","title":"Already enrolled","status":409,"detail":"You are already enrolled in crs_42."}

(C) POST /orders -> 402
{"error":{"code":"CARD_DECLINED","msg":"The card was declined."}}

Statement: "The banner shows the text undefined for (B) and (C), and for (A) it shows both validation messages joined by a comma."
